The standard deviation of `a` is `1.58114`, so `1.58114 >= 1.65` doesn't hold, if only just, and step 1 fails. In step 2, `tol=0.05` allows 5% of the target (`0.0825`), so the standard deviation only has to be at least `1.5675`, and the step passes.

The target can also be the same aggregate of another column, given with
[`col()`](`pointblank.col`):

::: {#a0dcac07 .cell execution_count=7}
``` {.python .cell-code}
validation = (
    pb.Validate(data=tbl)
    .col_sd_ge(columns="a", value=pb.col("b"))
    .interrogate()
)

