With `reference=` set, leaving out `value=` compares against the same column in the reference table. Step 1 checks `25.0684 >= 26.1454` (the standard deviation of `revenue` in `current`, then in `baseline`), so it fails. Step 2 names the target column with [`ref()`](`pointblank.ref`), which you'd need if the column had a different name in the reference table, and allows a 5% tolerance, so it passes. Comparing each new load of a table with the last one known to be good like this catches drift that no single row would reveal.
